  abstract={This paper studies deterministic Hamiltonian dynamics on finite metric graphs. Since energy conservation alone does not determine how a trajectory continues through a branching vertex, the paper introduces energy-preserving vertex scattering maps. The resulting edge-and-vertex dynamics define a global measurable flow that preserves energy and the quotient Liouville measure.}
